From 7d690fcf2b2e93862769f0a32eb8965340499d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taher Shawki <taher.shawki@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:44:32 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(terminal): stream foreground command output

Add an optional output observer to the bounded process collector and wire foreground local terminal calls to session-scoped gateway events. Redact chunks before sending and suppress streaming when identical commands are running concurrently, so output cannot cross tool calls. Register a typed terminal.output event and test that observers receive chunks without affecting capture. This preserves command execution and approval behavior; remote terminal backends keep their existing output behavior.
